## Swap Settings

<!-- '#' field names: /update.php ignores them, so Apply/Default never touch the swap
     settings. Only 'Create swapfile' stores them (exec.php) - the cfg always describes the
     swapfile that really exists. -->

_(Size in GB, 1-128)_:
: <input type="number" name="#size_gb" min="1" max="128" value="<?=$h('size_gb')?>">

> Size of the swapfile in gigabytes. There is no resize: disable swap, change the
> size and create it again - the old swapfile gets replaced. Creating writes the
> full size to the disk, so make sure the pool has enough free space.

_(Path)_:
: <input type="text" name="#location" class="narrow" value="<?=$h('location')?>" placeholder="/mnt/cache/system/swap">

> Directory that holds the swapfile, for example /mnt/cache/system/swap. Use a
> direct pool path and never /mnt/user (FUSE overlay) or network shares: the
> kernel refuses swapfiles there. The pool must be mounted and must match the
> selected filesystem, otherwise creation refuses. The share must not have a mover
> action that moves files off this disk (the mover would move the active swapfile);
> such locations are refused. A hidden top-level directory such as
> /mnt/cache/.swap is never touched by the mover.

_(File name)_:
: <input type="text" name="#name" value="<?=$h('name')?>">

> File name of the swapfile inside the path. Only letters, digits, dot, dash
> and underscore are allowed.

_(Filesystem)_:
: <select name="#fs">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['fs'], 'auto', _('auto (detected at the path)'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['fs'], 'zfs', 'zfs (zvol)')?>
  </select>

> auto detects the filesystem really mounted under the path (xfs/ext4:
> swapfile directly; btrfs: only single device and nocow). Swapfiles on
> other filesystems (FAT, tmpfs, ...) are refused. zfs: swap files are not
> supported, the plugin creates a zvol (block device) instead.

_(ZFS pool, only for zfs)_:
: <input type="text" name="#zpool" value="<?=$h('zpool')?>">

> Name of the ZFS pool that holds the zvol. Only used when the filesystem is
> zfs. Note: per the OpenZFS FAQ even a zvol as swap is not deadlock-safe on
> Linux, so prefer an xfs pool where possible.

_(vm.swappiness, 0-200)_:
: <input type="number" name="#swappiness" class="narrow" min="0" max="200" value="<?=$h('swappiness')?>">

> Kernel setting vm.swappiness (0-200): how eagerly the kernel moves memory
> pages to swap. A low value like 10 keeps swap as an emergency buffer, higher
> values swap out more aggressively. The buttons below the field reset it to
> the default (10) or save and apply it immediately. The value is set whenever
> this plugin enables swap.

<input type="button" value="_(Default)_" onclick="swapSwappinessDefault()">
: <input type="button" value="_(Save swappiness)_" onclick="swapSwappiness()">

_(Binding)_:
: <select name="#bind_mode">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['bind_mode'], 'direct', _('direct (recommended)'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['bind_mode'], 'loop', _('loop device (workaround, not recommended)'))?>
  </select>

> direct is the recommended path. loop is only for btrfs multi-device/RAID
> pools where the kernel refuses a direct swapfile; it bypasses the check but
> not the reason behind it and carries a stall risk under memory pressure -
> see the full warning below.

## History Settings

<!-- '#' field names as above: Apply/Default of General never touch them, only the
     buttons of this section store them (exec.php, action=history_settings) -->

_(Usage history)_:
: <select name="#history">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['history'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['history'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

> When enabled, a background sampler records the swap usage (in RAM, at most 24
> hours; it starts over after a reboot). It is the system-wide swap usage of all
> active swap devices (e.g. also a zram swap from another plugin), not only the
> swapfile of this plugin; the same applies to the dashboard ring. The graph below and the dashboard tile
> show it; the dashboard then shows the graph instead of the usage ring (reload
> the dashboard after changing this). Disabling stops the sampler and deletes the
> recorded history.

_(Sampling interval in seconds, min. 5 seconds)_:
: <input type="number" name="#history_interval" class="narrow" min="5" step="1" value="<?=$h('history_interval')?>">

> How often the swap usage is sampled. Smaller values give a finer graph for short
> ranges (5 minutes at 30 s = 10 points), larger values cost less.

_(Graph range)_:
: <select name="#history_range">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['history_range'], '300', _('5 minutes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['history_range'], '3600', _('1 hour'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['history_range'], '86400', _('24 hours'))?>
  </select>

> Time range shown by the graph below and by the dashboard tile. Long ranges show
> the peak per point, so short spikes stay visible.

> The buttons below reset the history fields to their defaults or save and apply
> them immediately (the sampler is restarted with the new interval).

<input type="button" value="_(Default)_" onclick="swapHistoryDefault()">
